    "Bounded soft-chroma/channel recovery atlases precede more expensive field expansion; successful first reads keep their established path.",
    "Exact names and signed percentages retain independent evidence/confidence. One signed percentage may have bounded punctuation; missing signs, extra digits/values and contradictions stay unverified.",
    "The first live War read with colour inference enabled can display five usable known rows provisionally before field expansion and standard fallback; subsequent retries retain the stronger path and verification rules.",
